alk  about the structure of the mentorship  program and my experience through it so  I meet with Allison and I Elementary's  weekly and then we go over like my  project I'm doing any trouble are having  with coding and they're like approaches  for me I want to build something then  how should I approach this problem and a  lot of things like that so I think that  from my learning experience the book the  elementary introduction to the Wolfram  language book is a really great place to  start it has a lot of really great  example step-by-step kind of examples on  each concept and also the development  platform is like a free online platform  one can sign in for free and they can  just start playing around with code and  it's connect to the programming lab  which is I think is really helpful  because I I try it out using that and it  has all these exploration  on how you can do like for example the  circle escapes I showed before was from  there where you can just it'll show you  how to do a lot of cool things using  code and it's basically made a made so  that kids can learn how to explore  around with code and play around it  within themselves yeah so I would just  like to give a special thanks to dr.  Wolfram for introducing me to the  monstrous program and then my mentors  from Wolfram Allison John and Todd yeah  so thank you  [Applause]
 

